---
/*
  ============================================================
  DIRECT VARIANT — /variants/direct/
  ============================================================
  Positioning vs the parallel agents:
    - Substance lean: publication-quiet, essay-shaped.
    - Polariser lean: sharp-contrarian, opinionated.
    - This page (Direct):  clean, structured, deliverable-forward.
      Reads like an SOW landing page. Specificity over poetry.

  Design decisions documented inline:

  FONT:
    Heads + numerals: 'IBM Plex Sans' — geometric, structured,
      reads as engineering / spec rather than marketing. Slightly
      narrower than Inter, gives a documents-and-deliverables feel.
    Body:             'Inter' (already in global.css) — familiar,
      readable at the long-form pricing/about sections.
    Mono accent:      'IBM Plex Mono' for week labels and price
      numerals — anchors the page in deliverable-spec territory.
    Loaded via a <link> tag injected directly in this page;
      Astro hoists <link rel> from anywhere in the template into
      <head>, so this is safe and stays scoped to /variants/direct/.

  COLOR:
    Stay on the 'main' theme tokens (warm orange accent on near-
    white) so we inherit nav + footer treatments cleanly, but
    locally override --accent to a flatter ink-blue (#1F4ED8) and
    --bg to a slightly cooler off-white (#F7F7F5). Reasoning:
      - Substance will likely sit on the warm/neutral palette;
        Polariser will likely use high-contrast / black.
      - Direct sits in between with a structured ink-blue accent
        that reads engineering/contract, not lifestyle.
    All overrides are scoped to .direct-variant via is:global so
    they never leak to other pages.

  ANIMATION:
    Reused .reveal from BaseLayout's IntersectionObserver. Added
    a single page-local IntersectionObserver to count up the week
    numbers in the timeline (W1, W2... animate from 0 -> n once).
    No parallax, no fancy easing — Direct is meant to feel like
    you can read it fast. Reduced-motion users see no counter
    animation; numbers render in their final state.

  CTA MECHANIC:
    The primary CTA ("free 5-page teardown") is a 3-field inline
    form posting to a mailto: handler — no JS submission, no
    third-party widget. Reasoning:
      - The newview/ page already embeds Calendly. Doing it again
        here would just be the same pattern. Direct says "give me
        five business days, I'll send a real artifact" — that's
        an asynchronous request, not a meeting.
      - The secondary CTA ("Book a scope call") IS a Calendly
        link-out (button, not embed). Embeds are heavy; we use one
        only where it's truly the next step. The scope call is for
        users who already chose the paid path.
    Form falls back to mailto on submit so the page works without
    a backend (this is a static GitHub Pages build).

  BASE LAYOUT: USED.
    BaseLayout gives us nav, IntersectionObserver, footer-friendly
    body padding, and theme switching. Skipping it would mean
    rebuilding the nav. Worth keeping.

  COPY:
    Used the mockup verbatim. Replaced ASCII button markers with
    real <a>/<button>. Bracketed placeholders ("[Brief origin...]"
    "[Once first case study lands...]") preserved as visible
    italic placeholders so the user can fill them in later.
    Removed nothing.
  ============================================================
*/
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const calendlyURL = 'https://calendly.com/follow_action/30min';
const teardownEmail = 'andrew@firstactionfix.com';

const footerLinks = [
  { label: 'Teardowns', href: '#proof' },
  { label: 'Writing',   href: '#proof' },
  { label: 'About',     href: '#about' },
  { label: 'Contact',   href: `mailto:${teardownEmail}` },
];

// Week-by-week timeline data
const weeks = [
  {
    label: 'W1–2',
    title: 'Audit',
    body: "Trial flow walkthrough. Signup-to-stall observation across real user cohorts. Instrumentation review. Gap analysis.",
    deliverable: '30-page diagnostic with prioritised recommendations.',
  },
  {
    label: 'W3–4',
    title: 'Build',
    body: "Educational Email Course (6 emails, ~12,000 words of structured curriculum specific to your category and your buyer's stage of awareness). Behavioral trigger sequence (8–12 triggers mapped to your activation-stall moments, defined in week 2's audit).",
    deliverable: 'Two paired email systems, drafted and reviewed.',
  },
  {
    label: 'W5',
    title: 'Implementation',
    body: 'Embedded with your team in your ESP and analytics stack. Pairing sessions twice a week. Live deployment.',
    deliverable: 'Both systems running against real trial signups.',
  },
  {
    label: 'W6',
    title: 'Handoff',
    body: 'Documentation. Dashboards. Trigger logic explained for the team that will own it after I leave. One follow-up call 30 days post-handoff.',
    deliverable: 'Full ownership transferred. 30-day follow-up call booked.',
  },
];

const goodFit = [
  'Sales engagement / cold email tooling',
  'Prospecting and lead enrichment',
  'CRM-adjacent automation',
  'Email deliverability infrastructure',
];

const wrongFit = [
  'Pre-product-market-fit',
  'Enterprise sales motion (no real PLG trial)',
  'Already have a competent in-house lifecycle email team',
  'Under 100 monthly trial signups (the EEC-only tier suits better)',
];
---

